From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Build: let the jobserver control the wxWidgets build

The wxbuild target always runs its sub-make with -j 4, which overrides
the job count and jobserver of the OpenWrt build. Inherit them instead.
OpenWrt-specific: a standalone upstream build would then build
wxWidgets serially unless make is called with -j.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenWrt specific]

Signed-off-by: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
---
 src/Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/Makefile
+++ b/src/Makefile
@@ -746,4 +746,4 @@ endif
 	"$(WX_ROOT)/configure" $(WX_CONFIGURE_FLAGS) $(WX_CONFIGURE_EXTRA_FLAGS) $$WX_CONFIGURE_LEGACY_FLAGS >/dev/null
 
 	@echo Building wxWidgets library...
-	cd "$(WX_BUILD_DIR)" && $(MAKE) -j 4
+	cd "$(WX_BUILD_DIR)" && $(MAKE)
